    {
      "id": "7773b949afbca125249c5a407eb08bddb10b0ade",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 609497293,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Is reset_find_package() documented anywhere, I couldn't find it?\n\nIt seems to be a bit brute force to effectively undo the caching of package info each time a generation is run, we might as well make the find_package calls to not cache.  With Windows we at least have the tag file which causes win-setup.ps1 to be run, this could call reset_find_package for all packages updated by the script.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6621762,
            "username": "graham.bloice",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Graham Bloice",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/8730bfac2267cb97ff1f8187d285f244745a03a783055c8fd6fcd679bfa71c6e?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/graham.bloice"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-06-23T13:15:48.906Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-06-23T13:15:48.906Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 105494391,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 3450,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "522e9af3c5e9981bdda15d4d231b13155c7a9312",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 610780973,
          "type": null,
          "body": "`reset_find_package` is something we added in Wireshark, see commit f54a6256820b96ad6d34955e87f7897d77d46983 for the context.\n\nThe cache is only cleared if the library cannot be located which usually indicates that it has been updated. If the library file still exists, it won't be cleared.\n\nIt's better than asking the user to manually blow their entire CMakeCache.txt.",
          "author": {
            "id": 2415432,
            "username": "Lekensteyn",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Peter Wu",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/efcf30db53f30b15e7c905ef37bd4dc44d87573bd92baf97cd707115d3fcd0c0?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/Lekensteyn"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-06-24T14:31:29.382Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-06-24T14:31:29.382Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 105494391,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 3450,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "11b137d09394d2489f1c97a322176daff6c678db",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 610805681,
          "type": null,
          "body": "`reset_find_package` had totally passed me by.  It's probably worked multiple times without me noticing.\n\nAs I didn't know where It came from I didn't know that it was a \"conditional.\" reset.  As it is, this seems fine to me.\n\nThere are a few other things that this could help, e.g. Python and Perl, but they don't change that often.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6621762,
            "username": "graham.bloice",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Graham Bloice",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
